  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Complete the square to find the centre and the radius of each circle.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2+4x+y^2+8y=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Centre $(-2,-4)$; radius $2\\sqrt{5}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^2+4x)+(y^2+8y)&=0\\\\(x^2+4x+4)+(y^2+8y+16)&=4+16\\\\(x+2)^2+(y+4)^2&=20\\end{align*}$$\nCentre $(-2,-4)$; radius $\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2+4x+2y-5=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Centre $(-2,-1)$; radius $\\sqrt{10}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^2+4x)+(y^2+2y)&=5\\\\(x^2+4x+4)+(y^2+2y+1)&=5+4+1\\\\(x+2)^2+(y+1)^2&=10\\end{align*}$$\nCentre $(-2,-1)$; radius $\\sqrt{10}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+2y^2-8x+5y+3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Centre $\\left(2,-\\frac54\\right)$; radius $\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}4$.\n\nDivide by $2$, then complete the square in both variables.",
          "worked": "Divide by $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+y^2-4x+\\frac52y+\\frac32&=0\\\\(x^2-4x)+\\left(y^2+\\frac52y\\right)&=-\\frac32\\\\(x^2-4x+4)+\\left(y^2+\\frac52y+\\frac{25}{16}\\right)&=-\\frac32+4+\\frac{25}{16}\\\\(x-2)^2+\\left(y+\\frac54\\right)^2&=\\frac{65}{16}\\end{align*}$$\nCentre $\\left(2,-\\frac54\\right)$; radius $\\sqrt{\\frac{65}{16}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2-4x+6y-37=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Centre $(2,-3)$; radius $5\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^2-4x)+(y^2+6y)&=37\\\\(x^2-4x+4)+(y^2+6y+9)&=37+4+9\\\\(x-2)^2+(y+3)^2&=50\\end{align*}$$\nCentre $(2,-3)$; radius $\\sqrt{50}=5\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      }
    ]
